<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Vierfontein yr shr edges up, no div.</title>
<headline>Vierfontein yr shr edges up, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - attrib		  0.8	   vs 0.5</p>
<p>    After tax profit	0.03	  vs 0.02</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   0.05	  vs 0.03</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.02	  vs 0.01</p>
<p>    Administration costs  0.04	  vs 0.05</p>
<p>    Interest received     0.09	  vs 0.07</p>
<p>Full name: Vierfontein Colliery Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said that no significant progress had been made in the past six months towards the issue of a closure certificate for the firm's colliery. In view of this it had been decided not to declare a dividend.</p>
<p>Vierfontein on June 2 said that Ben Nevis Holdings Ltd (BNH) has approached it with proposals which could result in a new business being placed in the colliery.</p>
<p>BNH had already acquired an 18 percent shareholding in Vierfontein and proposes to make a fully guaranteed cash offer to acquire all existing shares at a price of no less than 25 cents a share, the coal firm said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
